  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Partnership Building between the Irish and Tanzanian Criminal Justice Systems program&#x2013; Promotion of Improved Victim-Centred Approaches in the Handling of Child Sexual Abuse cases in Tanzania: With the proposed grant, IRLI will support cascading of trainings of both police and judiciary, nurture institutional links between Tanzania prosecutors and their counterparts in Ireland and conduct a criminal justice conference to strengthen partnerships and exchange best practice in investigating and adjudication of GBV and CSA cases.  In addition, they will continue to foster collaboration and mutual learning amongst justice actors in Tanzania, Ireland and Northern Ireland towards the improves handling of GBV and CSA cases.</narrative>
  </description>
